the writers behind Star Wars the rise of  Skywalker have got some explaining to do  Skywalker writer director JJ Abrams was  recently captured on video explaining to  a group of fans the oddly less than  defined relationship between Rey and  kylo Ren and Star Wars sequel films ever  since the release of Star Wars The Force  awakens there has been a significant  subset of fans call them the reloj  contingent who have been pining to see  the resistance fighter Rey and the first  order villain kylo just admit their  feelings for each other already there  has always been a strong chemistry  between the two which could easily be  taken for a romantic undertone to their  relationship despite the fact that for  most of the sequel trilogy the two were  playing for opposite teams during the  events of the rise of Skywalker Ren is  moved to discard his old lightsaber and  reclaim his original identity has been  solo son of Han and Leia and the former  pupil of Luke Skywalker  after Rey is seemingly killed during her  fight with Emperor Palpatine then  redeems himself by transferring his life  force to her saving her life before he  becomes one with the force  he kisses her seemingly vindicating  every fan who ever insisted there was  something going on between those two you  come from nothing you're nothing  from alchemy according to Abrams though  that something wasn't what we might have  thought it was is off-the-cuff  explanation of the relationship to a  group of fans was posted online by  Twitter user rise of kylo and it may  make you cringe just a little in the  video they posted Abram said there's as  much of a brother-sister thing between  kylo and Rey as there is a romantic  thing it's more like they're just bound  together in this crazy spiritual way  Abrams bolstered his argument by looking  to musical maestro john williams who  composed the music for Star Wars from  the very beginning before things got so  complicated between its main characters  but they'll make 